    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d623">

                <pb facs="0612" n="542" sameAs="frus:frus1934v04/pg542"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.3231/578a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gibson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-01-03T13:00:00-05:00">January 3, 1934—1
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2. Department’s 103, December 6, noon.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d623-f1"/> What
                    progress is being made? The Colombian treaty was signed December 15.<anchor
                        n="3" xml:id="d623-f2"/> We are most anxious to make progress with the
                    Brazilian treaty.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
